# Copy to scheduled.env (anywhere - deploy/ is a reasonable spot) and
# fill in real values. These are the *extra* env vars rain_alert.py and
# news_digest.py need beyond what's already in telegram_bot.env -
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID are reused as-is from
# there either way; BRAVE_API_KEY (used by news_digest_agent.py, via the
# real telegram_bot.Agent) or TAVILY_API_KEY (used by news_digest.py's
# own bespoke call) is too, whichever script you actually run.
#
# This file is sourced directly in the crontab command (see
# cron-notifications.md), not loaded by the scripts themselves - plain
# KEY=VALUE pairs, no quotes needed.

NTFY_TOPIC=your-ntfy-topic-here

# Optional - see rain_alert.py's and news_digest.py's own docstrings for
# what each defaults to if left unset:
# ALERT_LOCATION=Tokyo, Japan
# RAIN_THRESHOLD_MM=7.5
# NEWS_QUERY=top world news today

# Optional - see vocab_drip.py's own docstring for what each defaults to
# if left unset. vocab_drip.py also needs TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and
# TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHAT_ID, but those are already in ../telegram_bot.env.
# VOCAB_LEVEL=N3
# VOCAB_COUNT=4

# Optional - add each drip's words to a Notion database as one row PER
# WORD (browsable, filterable), alongside the Telegram push. Both vars
# must be set or the Notion step is skipped; failures are logged per row
# and the Telegram drip still goes out. The database needs a title
# property named 'Word'; it also fills these if present (exact names):
# Reading, Meaning, Particle, Example 1, Example 2, Example 3 (rich_text),
# Type, JLPT (select). Particle holds the 助詞 patterns. Share the
# database with the integration. Setup: cron-notifications.md.
# NOTION_API_KEY=secret_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# NOTION_VOCAB_DB_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional - also append each drip to a Google Doc, formatted as a
# NotebookLM source (preamble + Heading 2 per word + labelled fields +
# each example in Japanese / kana / English) for audio overviews,
# flashcards, infographics. Both vars must be set or the step is skipped;
# failures are logged, Telegram still goes out. GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON
# is a path to a service-account key file; share the target Doc with that
# account's client_email as Editor. Needs the google-auth package
# (requirements.txt). Setup: cron-notifications.md.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=/home/deploy/vocab-gdoc-sa.json
# VOCAB_GDOC_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
